                <h1>Quest Technical Specifications </h1><p>Northwestern has=
 regularly invested in<a href=3D"https://www.it.northwestern.edu/department=
s/it-services-support/research/computing/quest/index.html"> Quest</a>&nbsp;=
to refresh and expand computing resources to meet the needs of the research=
 community. This includes hundreds of nodes that are available free of char=
ge as <a href=3D"https://www.it.northwestern.edu/departments/it-services-su=
pport/research/computing/quest/quest-access-and-allocations.html#general-ac=
cess">General Access resources</a>, as well as Priority Access,&nbsp;<a hre=
f=3D"https://www.it.northwestern.edu/secure/purchasing-resources.html">purc=
hased resources</a>.</p>
<h2>Quest Storage</h2>
<p>Quest has an IBM GPFS parallel file system with ESS storage totaling app=
roximately 12 PB. All users have access to a small (80 GB) home directory. =
Users may also request storage resources to gain access to a project direct=
ory optimized for high-performance computing operations.</p>
<p>Users with access to computing resources on Quest will automatically be =
allocated 5 TB of scratch space that can be used for temporary file storage=
. Backed by a 500 TB flash disk drive, scratch space provides very high per=
formance for file operations. It is specific to the user=E2=80=99s NetID an=
d cannot be expanded beyond 5 TB. Files that haven=E2=80=99t been modified =
within 30 days are automatically removed from the scratch space.</p>
<p>Users who are only utilizing Quest Analytics and no other compute resour=
ces will need to submit a ticket to <a href=3D"mailto:quest-help@northweste=
rn.edu">quest-help@northwestern.edu</a> requesting scratch space.</p>
<h2>Compute Resources</h2>
<p>Quest comprises 7 login nodes and over 1300 compute nodes, with a total =
of over 90,000 cores. These nodes include over 107 GPU nodes and 30 high-me=
mory nodes. Both the login and compute nodes are running the Red Hat Enterp=
rise Linux 8.10 operating system.</p>
<h3>Regular Compute Nodes</h3>
<p>Quest currently consists of the following architectures:</p>
<p><strong>Quest 14 - Intel Emerald Rapids</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Number of Nodes: 60 nodes with 7,680 cores total, 128 cores per node</l=
i>
<li>Processor: Intel(R) Xeon(R) Platinum 8592+ CPU @ 1.9GHz</li>
<li>Memory: Per node (per core) 512 GB (4 GB), Type: DDR5 5600 MHz</li>
<li>Interconnect: Infiniband HDR</li>
<li>Expected retirement: Fall 2031</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Quest 13 - Intel Emerald Rapids</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Number of Nodes: 140 nodes with 17920 cores total, 128 cores per node</=
li>
<li>Processor: Intel(R) Xeon(R) Platinum 8592+ CPU @ 1.9GHz</li>
<li>Memory: Per node (per core) 512 GB (4 GB), Type: DDR5 5600 MHz</li>
<li>Interconnect: Infiniband HDR</li>
<li>Expected retirement: Spring 2030</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Quest 12 - Intel Ice Lake</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Number of Nodes: 214 nodes with 13696 cores total, 64 cores per node</l=
i>
<li>Processor: Intel(R) Xeon(R) Gold 6338 CPU @ 2.0GHz</li>
<li>Memory: Per node (per core) 256 GB (4 GB), Type: DDR4 3200 MHz</li>
<li>Interconnect: Infiniband HDR</li>
<li>Expected retirement: Fall 2028</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Quest 11 - Intel Ice Lake</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Number of Nodes: 209 nodes with 13376 cores total, 64 cores per node</l=
i>
<li>Processor: Intel(R) Xeon(R) Gold 6338 CPU @ 2.0GHz</li>
<li>Memory: Per node (per core) 256 GB (4 GB), Type: DDR4 3200 MHz</li>
<li>Interconnect: Infiniband HDR Compatible</li>
<li>Expected retirement: Fall 2027</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Quest 10 - Intel Cascade Lake</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Number of Nodes: 555 nodes with 28860 cores total, 52 cores per node</l=
i>
<li>Processor: Intel(R) Xeon(R) Gold 6230 CPU @ 2.10GHz</li>
<li>Memory: Per node (per core) 192 GB (3.7 GB), Type: DDR4 2933MHz</li>
<li>Interconnect: Infiniband EDR</li>
<li>Expected retirement: Fall 2026</li>
</ul>
<h3>GPU Nodes</h3>
<p>Quest has a total of 317 GPU cards on 107&nbsp;<a href=3D"https://www.it=
.northwestern.edu/departments/it-services-support/research/computing/gpu/in=
dex.html">GPU nodes</a> across General Access and Priority Access resources=
. GPUs available to General Access resources:</p>
<p><strong>Quest 13 - Intel Emerald Rapids with NVIDIA H100 GPUs</strong></=
p>
<ul>
<li>Number of Nodes: 24 nodes with 1536 cores total, 64 cores per node</li>
<li>Processor: Intel(R) Xeon(R) Platinum 8562Y+ CPU @ 2.8 GHz (Emerald Rapi=
ds)</li>
<li>Memory: Per node (Per Core) 1 TB (16 GB), Type: DDR5 5600 MHz</li>
<li>GPU cards per node: 4 x 80 GB NVIDIA H100 (Connected with SXM5 and HBM3=
)</li>
<li>Interconnect: Infiniband NDR</li>
<li>Expected retirement: Fall 2029</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Quest 12 - Intel Ice Lake with NVIDIA A100 GPUs</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Number of Nodes: 18 nodes with 1152 cores total, 64 cores per node</li>
<li>Processor: Intel(R) Xeon(R) Gold 6338 CPU @ 2.0 GHz (Ice Lake)</li>
<li>Memory: Per node (Per Core) 512 GB (8 GB), Type: DDR4 3200 MHz</li>
<li>GPU cards per node: 4 x 80 GB NVIDIA A100 (Connected with SXM4 and HBM2=
)</li>
<li>Interconnect: Infiniband HDR</li>
<li>Expected retirement: Fall 2028</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Quest 10 - Intel Cascade Lake with NVIDIA A100 GPUs</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Number of Nodes: 16 nodes with 832 cores total, 52 cores per node=E2=80=
=AF</li>
<li>Processor: Intel(R) Xeon(R) Gold 6230 CPU @ 2.10 GHz=E2=80=AF (Cascade =
Lake)</li>
<li>Memory: Per node (Per Core) 192 GB (3.7 GB), Type: DDR4 2933 MHz</li>
<li>GPU cards per node: 2 x 40 GB NVIDIA A100 (Connected with PCIe)</li>
<li>Interconnect: Infiniband HDR</li>
<li>Expected retirement: Fall 2026</li>
</ul>
<p>Quest GPU resources can support multiple versions of the modern CUDA Too=
lkit. More information is available&nbsp;in the&nbsp;<a href=3D"https://rcd=
sdocs.it.northwestern.edu/systems/quest/user-guide/gpu/gpu.html">Quest GPU =
documentation</a>.&nbsp;</p>
<h3>High-Memory Nodes</h3>
<p>Quest has 12 General Access high-memory nodes: four with 52 cores and 1.=
5 TB memory, six with 128 cores and 1 TB memory, and two with 128 cores and=
 2 TB memory.&nbsp; For more information on how to run jobs on a high-memor=
y node, see <a href=3D"https://rcdsdocs.it.northwestern.edu/systems/quest/u=
ser-guide/slurm/slurm.html#partitions">Quest Partitions/Queues</a>. High-me=
mory nodes can be <a href=3D"https://www.it.northwestern.edu/departments/it=
-services-support/research/computing/quest/index.html#dedicated-access">pur=
chased&nbsp;for Priority Access</a> on Quest.</p>
